    "created_at": "2026-11-27T13:32:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T13:32:23Z",
    "body": "Profile of the rotor import, from the instrumentation in PR #4374 (release, Windows x64, Rotor.STEP 3.7 MB, one solid, 58 faces):\n\n- read_step: ~20 s (parse 33 ms, guards 3 ms, topology read 16.5 s, build 3.4 s)\n- mesh at 0.005 mm: plan 64.0 s + redivide 12.3 s + deviation 126.8 s, replan at 2.5e-3 mm plan 37.2 s - refused (face 35 capped): ~240 s\n- mesh at 0.01 mm, attempt 1: plan 18.0 s + redivide 2.4 s + deviation 167.4 s - rejected (1.79e-2 mm over tolerance): ~188 s\n- mesh at 0.01 mm, attempt 2 (chord 5e-3): plan 64.8 s + redivide 12.3 s + deviation 114.5 s + facets 0.85 s + weld 0.4 s - success, 5,830,496 triangles: ~195 s\n\nTotal ~640 s of work before a mesh is handed out; the 300 s watchdog cancels mid-way.\n\nDominant stage: mesh_deviation (115-167 s per attempt, 88-95M samples over 5.8M triangles, our code). Next: mesh_plan (18-65 s, pinned solidcore).\n\nRecommended fix: a seam-level pre-pass (measure per face as the plan is built, refuse a doomed plan early) and starting at the loose chord (the 0.005 mm attempt always ends refused). A pin move helps only the 36 s of topology+plan; per-solid parallelism does not help (one solid).",
